WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.330
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.220
He's here!

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.180
That's Hanoi!

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.940
What is it?  I was just explaining Hanoi-

00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.420
Show up, Playmaker!

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:31.680
Hey, everyone!

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:34.500
I brought presents!

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.800
Hey!

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.630
Nobody's here?

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.240
Where is everyone?

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:15.290
Until yesterday, they only had eyes for me.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.530
But now, they only have eyes for Playmaker!

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:44.680
I run Across the universe

00:01:44.830 --> 00:01:47.850
At the speed of light

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:49.720
Begin Loading

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:53.450
Open the door of dreams

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:57.020
VRAINS spreads

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:00.130
Believe in myself

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.660
VRAINS continues

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:08.970
The circuit draws the future

00:02:09.250 --> 00:02:13.040
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:14.640
Access!

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:17.340
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:18.950
I'm now With the Wind

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.250
Link with my soul

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.020
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.750
Now Win the Race

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.590
Connected world

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.090
No matter when

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:35.460
Nothing is impossible

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:39.600
Strive for hope

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:44.170
And ride the wind!

00:03:14.110 --> 00:03:15.020
Here I go!

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:21.310
Yes!  This wind is for Speed Dueling!

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:26.560
Large Data Storm ahead.  Please be careful.

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:33.890
Who do you think you're 
talking to?  I'm Go Onizuka!

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.220
Working hard, I see.

00:03:51.580 --> 00:03:53.070
Yeah.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.550
The battlefield may be different, 
but I'm still a champion.

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:03.420
For saving LINK VRAINS, the world 
treats Playmaker like a hero.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.840
That's only for now.

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.190
The winner of a duel becomes a hero.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:13.240
Exactly!  In this world, 
the winner is the hero.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:20.910
Some say your dueling style is 
old-fashioned, but don't worry about that.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:27.480
Right...  I want them to 
look at me like that again.

00:04:30.260 --> 00:04:34.140
I just want the kids to cheer for me again!

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:38.090
But the problem is: Will 
he agree to duel you?

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.090
You're right.

00:04:49.030 --> 00:04:51.820
If you can retrieve the Ignis...

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:54.940
...I don't care if your dueling style is old.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:58.120
A duelist who can defeat Playmaker.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.800
That's right.

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.400
I'm the only duelist who can.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:09.020
Mr. Onizuka!  How nice of you to visit me.

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:15.590
If there's anything you desire, 
I'm prepared to accept.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:21.600
I only want you to create a location within 
LINK VRAINS where I can battle him.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:26.570
I want to be known as the 
man who defeated Playmaker.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.600
Understood.  I promise to do so.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:54.970
Yusaku!  You forgot something.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:56.700
Right.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:02.640
Ooooh!

00:06:02.860 --> 00:06:04.960
A little more to the right!

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:08.600
Yes!  Right there!  Don't stop!

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:11.690
Please be quiet.  Or my 
hands will be off-position.

00:06:12.060 --> 00:06:14.650
Jeez.  You really are stupid.

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:17.020
That is a forbidden word.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.490
He shouldn't be back from school yet!

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:34.570
You're home early-

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.820
We're going to LINK VRAINS.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.500
Going?  To do what?

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:41.050
Knight of Hanoi has appeared.

00:06:41.050 --> 00:06:43.420
You're using me as a hostage again?

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:51.590
Oh my!  I didn't know you had this room!

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:57.030
Deck set!  Into the VRAINS!

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:29.030
You've arrived, Playmaker.

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.970
Sense something, Playmaker?

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:39.940
He's not a Knight of Hanoi.

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.910
I agree.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:50.370
I used the Knights of Hanoi to draw you out.

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:54.640
I'm Go Onizuka.

00:07:54.640 --> 00:08:00.260
The real hero has arrived 
to unmask the fake hero!

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:02.970
Searching Go Onizuka...

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.510
Entertainer who has conquered the duel world.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.970
Currently ranked #1 among Charisma Duelists!

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:11.880
I'm not interested.

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:12.640
Oh.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:27.110
Be careful.  This program blocks you 
from logging out of LINK VRAINS.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:29.880
Figured it out?

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:34.750
You can only undo this 
program by defeating me.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:38.600
Who hired you?

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:41.800
I'm not telling a hacker.

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:47.570
I just need to prove that I'm 
stronger than you, Playmaker.

00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:50.540
He's strong.  Don't let your guard down.

00:08:51.020 --> 00:08:52.570
I won't lose.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:10.160
It's SOL Technologies' program.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:13.460
My job is to remove it.

00:09:17.490 --> 00:09:20.330
Seize the wind, Playmaker!

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:30.540
Speed Duel!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:36.020
I go first!  My turn!

00:09:38.280 --> 00:09:42.030
I summon Gouki Suprex from my hand!

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:52.000
When Suprex is summoned, I can 
Special Summon a Gouki from my hand.

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:55.570
I play Gouki Twistcobra!

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:05.020
I end my turn.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:09.000
Let's see how much of an entertainer he is.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.150
I don't care.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:13.160
I'll defeat him by dueling my way.

00:10:15.840 --> 00:10:17.100
My turn!

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:22.600
I set one card.

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:30.840
When there are no monsters on my field, 
I can Special Summon this card.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:32.710
Come, Linkslayer!

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:41.690
Next, I summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:50.200
He's facing Go Onizuka?

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:53.300
It's about time for a new hero.

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.970
You think?

00:10:54.970 --> 00:11:00.540
But I love how Go Onizuka duels, making 
huge comebacks from the brink of defeat.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:05.040
No no!  That dueling style is last gen.

00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:07.910
Let's go, Playmaker!  My new hero!

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:10.980
Defeat Go Onizuka!

00:11:10.980 --> 00:11:18.700
The duel between Charisma Duelist Go Onizuka 
and LINK VRAINS's new hero Playmaker has begun!

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:22.970
Has Go Onizuka changed 
from a babyface to a heel?

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:28.700
Or will he "unmask the fake hero"?

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:33.040
Don't take your eyes off this duel!

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:35.120
Playmaker!

00:11:35.120 --> 00:11:37.340
The hero who protects LINK VRAINS!

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.410
Good luck, Playmaker!

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.190
They're very excited.

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:45.710
Onizuka is always nice to them, but...

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:47.150
I'm sorry.

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.150
Children tell the truth.

00:11:49.150 --> 00:11:52.620
They naturally cheer for the cool hero.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:58.600
Yes.  But if Onizuka wins as usual, 
they'll cheer for him again.

00:11:58.930 --> 00:12:02.420
Go Onizuka's duel is entertainment style.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:07.800
If the opponent's skill is a 5, he makes it 
look like an 8 or a 9 to make it more exciting.

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:09.950
Then he crushes them with a 10.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:14.840
That's how he'll defeat Playmaker.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.780
I found it.

00:12:22.280 --> 00:12:25.020
This is the program that's blocking him.

00:12:25.360 --> 00:12:27.000
This will be tough.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:29.530
It'll take some time to break it.

00:12:33.330 --> 00:12:35.970
I know!  I could do this!

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:38.970
If I put an escape route here...

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.410
Go Onizuka is baffling.

00:12:52.410 --> 00:12:57.190
He takes his opponent's attacks to 
put himself in danger on purpose.

00:12:57.780 --> 00:13:00.290
I have no desire to duel like that.

00:13:03.800 --> 00:13:06.430
We each have two monsters on the field.

00:13:07.310 --> 00:13:11.200
It's like a pro wrestling tag match!

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:16.720
Pro wrestling is my forte.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:22.510
I'll get the 1-2-3 count and win!

00:13:23.100 --> 00:13:24.620
We'll see about that.

00:13:24.960 --> 00:13:29.280
Cyberse Wizard uses its effect on Suprex!

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:31.220
He switches to defense position!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.530
Cyberse Algorithm!

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:37.530
What?

00:13:38.930 --> 00:13:43.370
Due to this effect, I can only attack 
the target monster this turn.

00:13:43.370 --> 00:13:45.840
But I can deal piercing damage.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:48.110
Go, Linkslayer!

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.410
Gouki Suprex has 0 DEF.

00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:57.180
You take damage equal to 
Linkslayer's 2000 ATK!

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.150
Meteor Slash!

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:20.000
Go Onizuka volunteers and 
donates to orphanages.

00:14:20.310 --> 00:14:22.520
Why does he do that?

00:14:23.520 --> 00:14:27.820
Oh!  He lived in that 
orphanage when he was a kid.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:33.240
He did it!

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:36.920
Playmaker is cool!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:41.430
He's entertainment dueling to earn money.

00:14:41.430 --> 00:14:44.880
Because the children's futures are at stake.

00:14:44.880 --> 00:14:45.860
I see, I see.

00:14:50.680 --> 00:14:55.760
If Gouki Twistcobra uses his 
effect, he can power himself up.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:15:00.110
That effect could've also negated the battle.

00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:04.400
That's right.  He took damage on purpose.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:11.660
I forgot to tell you of 
Go Onizuka's other trait.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:17.260
He puts himself in bad situations on purpose 
to entertain the crowd, but he never loses.

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:23.230
Just when he's about to lose, he makes 
a huge comeback to fire up the crowd.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:30.530
Onizuka...

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:32.910
Don't worry, Teacher.

00:15:34.180 --> 00:15:38.300
What you're seeing proves 
that he's in great shape.

00:15:38.300 --> 00:15:40.750
Go is about to do something amazing.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:43.750
Onizuka can't stand up!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.720
Playmaker wins.

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:49.760
Whoa!  Go Onizuka has 
been pushed to the brink!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:53.390
If this was wrestling, both 
his shoulders are on the mat!

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:55.970
The referee will strike the mat!

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:58.940
Let's do the three count!

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:01.370
One!

00:16:03.040 --> 00:16:04.810
Two!

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:08.620
Three-

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.720
No!  That's...

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:20.840
Whoa!  Go Onizuka raised 
his shoulders at 2.9!

00:16:22.170 --> 00:16:26.100
By going from the field to the 
graveyard, Suprex's effect activates!

00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:30.650
I can add a different Gouki 
in my deck to my hand.

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:35.570
I add Gouki Riscorpio to my hand!

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:39.240
He was pretending to lose.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.050
He's planning his next move.

00:16:42.320 --> 00:16:47.400
But since he lost 2000 LP, he took damage.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:52.260
Why did he take that attack on purpose?

00:16:54.280 --> 00:16:57.860
Humans take actions that are 
impossible to understand.

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:03.200
Yeah.  Because irrational actions 
can affect people's hearts.

00:17:03.200 --> 00:17:05.660
Huh?  What do you mean?

00:17:05.660 --> 00:17:07.530
It's pointless to explain to you.

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:09.870
You're so annoying!

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:16.580
Power...  Power is gathering in this arm!

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:21.820
All right!  I'm fired up!

00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:25.990
I activate my skill, Fighting Spirit!

00:17:26.300 --> 00:17:32.400
Fighting Spirit lets me Special Summon 
all Goukis destroyed in battle this turn!

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:36.940
My turn.

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.620
I draw!

00:17:39.360 --> 00:17:45.870
Due to Gouki Riscorpio's effect, I can 
summon it from my hand without tributing!

00:17:55.020 --> 00:17:57.860
He's completely back from the brink.

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:01.830
No.  He still hasn't shown 
his secret strategy.

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:07.300
Appear, my circuit!

00:18:16.530 --> 00:18:21.610
Whoa!  Link Summon will break the rules!

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:23.080
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:26.850
I need at least two Gouki monsters to summon!

00:18:26.850 --> 00:18:33.980
I set Suprex, Twistcobra and 
Riscorpio in the Link Markers!

00:18:36.750 --> 00:18:38.570
Circuit combine!

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.850
Link Summon!

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:55.250
Appear, Link 3 Gouki The Great Ogre!

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:02.770
What's going on?

00:19:02.770 --> 00:19:05.510
Go doesn't duel just to win.

00:19:05.510 --> 00:19:07.670
He also entertains the viewers.

00:19:07.670 --> 00:19:09.870
That's his style.

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:11.570
What'll happen next?

00:19:12.100 --> 00:19:15.530
In this duel, Go is in the lead.

00:19:15.880 --> 00:19:18.540
I knew Onizuka was awesome!

00:19:18.540 --> 00:19:21.010
Onizuka, you can do it!

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:24.400
You can do it, Onizuka!

00:19:27.150 --> 00:19:30.950
Go Onizuka is a true entertainer.

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:35.660
I need to hurry and create 
Yusaku's escape route.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:44.080
How's that!  Do you like my dueling?

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:51.000
What will you do, Playmaker?

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:56.830
Go Onizuka, finish this battle 
and retrieve the Ignis.

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:03.980
By going from the field to the 
graveyard, Gouki's effect activates!

00:20:04.200 --> 00:20:08.110
I can add a different Gouki 
in my deck to my hand.

00:20:08.660 --> 00:20:11.460
This is far from over.

00:20:11.460 --> 00:20:14.740
When Great Ogre is in the Monster Zone...

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:20.930
...all faceup monsters lose 
ATK equal to their DEF!

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:24.570
Take this!  Ogre Pressure!

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:35.100
What?  He even lowered our ATK?

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:39.920
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Gouki Re-Match!

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:45.420
I Special Summon two Goukis in my graveyard 
with different Levels in defense position!

00:20:47.120 --> 00:20:51.130
Not only did he Link Summon, 
he strengthened his defenses.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:56.460
You're making a mistake if you think 
he's just a flashy entertainer.

00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:59.050
This still isn't what he's aiming for.

00:21:00.160 --> 00:21:02.570
Twistcobra's effect activates!

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:12.350
By tributing Riscorpio, Great Ogre gains 
his ATK until the end of the turn!

00:21:14.720 --> 00:21:18.990
If you're attacked, you'll take 3900 damage!

00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:20.990
You'll only have 100 LP left!

00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:23.520
You should be a bit more scared!

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:29.840
This match is over.

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:38.670
I discard Twistcobra to Special Summon <i>Gouki 
Headbutt</i> from my hand in defense position!

00:21:43.780 --> 00:21:50.690
Due to <i>Headbutt's</i> effect, Great Ogre 
gains 800 ATK until the end of the turn!

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:57.390
This is my finisher!

00:22:24.470 --> 00:22:27.480
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.740 --> 00:22:31.020
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:34.620
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.940 --> 00:22:38.660
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:40.580 --> 00:22:42.580
Try It over and over

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:50.740
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:51.090 --> 00:22:57.680
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.970 --> 00:23:00.240
Nothing is certain

00:23:00.370 --> 00:23:01.920
In these isolated times

00:23:02.210 --> 00:23:03.650
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:05.420
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.680 --> 00:23:08.850
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.980 --> 00:23:12.420
The traces we leave behind

00:23:12.620 --> 00:23:16.390
The miracles we create

00:23:16.650 --> 00:23:18.600
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:18.600 --> 00:23:22.440
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:40.090 --> 00:23:46.970
The frantic back-and-forth Link Summons 
in the ring grab the children's attention.

00:23:47.230 --> 00:23:52.960
With a final clash, the three 
count rings across LINK VRAINS.

00:23:53.180 --> 00:23:55.500
Who's left standing in the end?

00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:58.160
I'll defeat him with superior dueling.

00:23:58.160 --> 00:24:00.320
That's my style!

00:24:00.960 --> 00:24:05.370
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
The Three Count Rings

00:24:05.370 --> 00:24:07.820
Into the VRAINS!
